      "message": "[error] Line 130: 🔴 `showWideOnly(_:)` has inverted guard logic, so visibility updates are skipped exactly when the wide-only controls should toggle. Starting state is hidden (`showWideOnly(false)`), and when width becomes wide, `guard self.wideOnly.first?.isHidden \u003d\u003d isWide else { return }` returns early, leaving controls hidden permanently. This is a functional regression in the new layout behavior. Compare against the desired hidden state (`!isWide`) instead, e.g. `let shouldHide \u003d !isWide; guard self.wideOnly.first?.isHidden !\u003d shouldHide else { return }`, then apply `isHidden \u003d shouldHide`.",
